# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Pages applies every rule whose path matches, so a page that matches two rules
# gets both. Where that would mean two Content-Security-Policy headers the browser
# enforces both at once, which is stricter than either. That is why the CSP below
# is set per page rather than globally: the guild, planner and gear pages get one,
# and the pages that carry advertising get none rather than a loose one that would
# have to be widened every time an ad network moves.
#
# Extensionless and .html paths are both listed. Pages serves /guild and
# /guild.html as the same page, and a rule for one does not cover the other.
#
# Nothing here can be tested from this repository. Verify it against the deployed
# site after a release: see RELEASE-BASELINE.md §5.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()

# The three pages that hold somebody's characters, a roster token, or a gear
# report. No advertising script runs on any of them, and this is what stops one
# being added back by accident.
#
# style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' because the pages set colours on elements as
# they draw them. script-src does not: every script on these pages is a file.
#
# connect-src names the bot exactly. img-src names Discord because an avatar in
# the header is served from their CDN. The fonts are served from here, so no
# stylesheet or font file leaves the site.
#
# static.cloudflareinsights.com is the one script from anywhere else, and it is
# not ours: Cloudflare injects its Web Analytics beacon into every page the zone
# serves. The first version of this policy blocked it, which took the page-view
# counts off these three pages and logged a violation on every load. It is
# cookieless and it is the same company already terminating TLS for every byte
# of this site, so allowing it costs nothing that has not already been spent.
#
# To make this strict again: turn Web Analytics off for the zone in the
# Cloudflare dashboard, then take both cloudflareinsights entries out of the
# policy below. Doing it in the other order leaves the console error behind.

/guild
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://cdn.discordapp.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.wowforever.us https://cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'

/guild.html
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://cdn.discordapp.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.wowforever.us https://cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'

